@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
!include style.iuml
title Operation - execution outcome and reconciliation
top to bottom direction
state Pending
state Completed
state Failed
state NeedsAttention
[*] --> Pending : record intended action
Pending --> Completed : execution confirms\naction and resulting facts
Pending --> Failed : execution fails\n[source remains; no destination]
Pending --> NeedsAttention : execution fails\n[outcome uncertain]
Pending --> Completed : recovery\n[only expected destination]
Pending --> Failed : recovery\n[only expected source]
Pending --> NeedsAttention : recovery\n[ambiguous, changed, unreadable]
NeedsAttention --> Completed : recovery\n[only expected destination]
NeedsAttention --> Failed : recovery\n[only expected source]
NeedsAttention --> NeedsAttention : recovery still\ninconclusive
note bottom of Completed
  An Undo is a new Operation.
  This completed record is retained.
end note
note bottom of Failed
  Retrying the original action creates a new Operation.
  No transition back to Pending for this attempt.
end note
legend bottom
  Expected = content matches the recorded fingerprint. Recovery does not move or delete copies.
  Recycle has no destination location: an intact expected source permits Failed;
  absence of the source remains NeedsAttention, not proof of recycling.
  Cancellation before recording creates no Operation. Unresolved attempts block the affected file/path.
endlegend
@enduml
